I've fixed the last open item on #1052: writing a file to a FIFO (a named pipe) no longer freezes yoyo's display. The fix is committed as 3281c288 with "Fixes #1052" in the title, so the issue closes when the commit is pushed.

What was wrong: before the write_file tool runs, yoyo reads the target's current content to show a diff preview. That read only checked that the path exists, and a FIFO exists, so the read blocked forever. yoagent's own refusal for non-regular files never got a chance to run.

Before the fix: I checked that the bug is real. A plain read of a FIFO did not return within 500 ms. A test (bare_read_of_the_fifo_fixture_blocks) now keeps that check in the suite, and it unblocks the pipe afterwards so it doesn't leave a stuck thread behind.

The fix: a small helper, preview_old_content, now does the read through the existing safe reader, which won't open non-regular files. It lives in a new file, src/prompt/write_preview.rs, so src/prompt.rs stays at 3905 lines and under its size cap.
• FIFOs and devices get no preview at all. Showing them as a "new file" diff would wrongly suggest a write that the tool is about to refuse. A comment in the code records this decision.
• Regular, missing and directory targets behave exactly as before. A regular file returns its exact content, so its diff is unchanged.

Tests: the FIFO case now returns immediately with no preview. It runs under a 5-second deadline, so a regression fails instead of hanging the suite. The regular-file and missing/empty/directory cases are also covered. These tests only run on Unix.

Proving the test catches the bug: I put the old read back temporarily, and exactly the FIFO test failed on its deadline. I restored the code in the same command and confirmed the temporary change was gone.

Checks: cargo fmt --check, cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings, the full cargo test run and the module-size gate all pass.

Also done:
• ARCHITECTURE.md said item 3 was still open; I corrected that and added an entry for this fix in the same commit.
• I commented on #1052 with the commit, the before/after measurements and the test result. The #1052 mentions in src/cli.rs and src/main.rs describe past fixes, not pending work, so I left them alone.
• --system-file <path> still isn't routed through the safe reader. That's deliberate and stated in the issue: --system-file <(cmd) is a FIFO the user chose.
